  "question": {
    "text": "Three rods of Copper, Brass and Steel are welded together to form a Y-shaped structure. Area of cross-section of each rod is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. End of copper rod is maintained at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. Where as ends of brass and steel are kept at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. Lengths of the copper, brass and steel rods are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>46</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cms</mi></math> respectively. The rods are thermally insulated from surroundings except at ends. Thermal conductivities of copper, brass and steel are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>26</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;CGS units respectively. Rate of heat flow through copper rod is :"
  },
